        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5NoyTFmbiUV2HVWiRSmj-27" parent="1" style="sketch=0;pointerEvents=1;shadow=0;dashed=0;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=#505050;labelPosition=center;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;outlineConnect=0;align=center;shape=mxgraph.office.concepts.video_play;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="70" width="110" x="910" y="2420" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5NoyTFmbiUV2HVWiRSmj-28" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;p data-start=&quot;179&quot; data-end=&quot;395&quot;&gt;“For storing video metadata and status (like &lt;em data-start=&quot;224&quot; data-end=&quot;262&quot;&gt;UPLOADING, PROCESSING, READY, FAILED&lt;/em&gt;), I would use a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;279&quot; data-end=&quot;307&quot;&gt;distributed SQL database&lt;/strong&gt; .&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;397&quot; data-end=&quot;833&quot;&gt;The reason is that video status is &lt;strong data-start=&quot;432&quot; data-end=&quot;460&quot;&gt;critical system metadata&lt;/strong&gt;, and we need &lt;strong data-start=&quot;474&quot; data-end=&quot;525&quot;&gt;strong consistency and transactional guarantees&lt;/strong&gt;. For example, when a user uploads a video, we first create a record with status &lt;em data-start=&quot;606&quot; data-end=&quot;617&quot;&gt;UPLOADING&lt;/em&gt;. Once the upload completes, the status changes to &lt;em data-start=&quot;668&quot; data-end=&quot;680&quot;&gt;PROCESSING&lt;/em&gt;, and after transcoding finishes it becomes &lt;em data-start=&quot;724&quot; data-end=&quot;731&quot;&gt;READY&lt;/em&gt;. We must ensure that users never see a partially processed video, so strong consistency is important.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;835&quot; data-end=&quot;869&quot;&gt;Distributed SQL databases provide:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul data-start=&quot;870&quot; data-end=&quot;1025&quot;&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;870&quot; data-end=&quot;893&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;872&quot; data-end=&quot;893&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;872&quot; data-end=&quot;893&quot;&gt;ACID transactions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;894&quot; data-end=&quot;922&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;896&quot; data-end=&quot;922&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;896&quot; data-end=&quot;922&quot;&gt;horizontal scalability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;923&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;925&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;925&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;high availability across regions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;962&quot; data-end=&quot;1025&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;964&quot; data-end=&quot;1025&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;964&quot; data-end=&quot;1025&quot;&gt;indexes for queries like videos by channel or upload time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1027&quot; data-end=&quot;1266&quot;&gt;To handle very high read traffic, I would place a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1077&quot; data-end=&quot;1138&quot;&gt;cache layer such as &lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Redis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; in front of the database so that frequently accessed metadata like video status, title, and manifest URL can be served quickly.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1268&quot; data-end=&quot;1297&quot;&gt;So the architecture would be:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1299&quot; data-end=&quot;1355&quot;&gt;Client → API → Redis Cache → Distributed SQL Metadata DB&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1357&quot; data-end=&quot;1456&quot;&gt;This ensures both &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1375&quot; data-end=&quot;1418&quot;&gt;low latency reads and consistent writes&lt;/strong&gt; for critical video state management.”&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="740" x="1410" y="1810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="5NoyTFmbiUV2HVWiRSmj-31" parent="1" style="image;sketch=0;aspect=fixed;html=1;points=[];align=center;fontSize=12;image=img/lib/mscae/SQL_Database_generic.svg;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="110" width="83.6" x="1285.24" y="1810" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
