        <UserObject label="&lt;p data-start=&quot;85&quot; data-end=&quot;458&quot;&gt;“The &lt;strong data-start=&quot;90&quot; data-end=&quot;108&quot;&gt;manifest files&lt;/strong&gt; used for adaptive streaming (HLS &lt;code data-start=&quot;142&quot; data-end=&quot;149&quot;&gt;.m3u8&lt;/code&gt; or DASH &lt;code data-start=&quot;158&quot; data-end=&quot;164&quot;&gt;.mpd&lt;/code&gt;) are stored in the same &lt;strong data-start=&quot;189&quot; data-end=&quot;207&quot;&gt;object storage&lt;/strong&gt; where the encoded video segments are stored. Large video platforms such as &lt;strong data-start=&quot;283&quot; data-end=&quot;324&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; typically use distributed object storage like &lt;strong data-start=&quot;371&quot; data-end=&quot;412&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Google Cloud Storage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong data-start=&quot;416&quot; data-end=&quot;457&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;460&quot; data-end=&quot;748&quot;&gt;During the video processing pipeline, after transcoding the raw video into multiple resolutions (for example 360p, 720p, 1080p), the system splits the video into small segments. At the same time, it generates the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;673&quot; data-end=&quot;690&quot;&gt;manifest file&lt;/strong&gt; which lists all available bitrates and segment locations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;750&quot; data-end=&quot;796&quot;&gt;The storage structure usually looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;798&quot; data-end=&quot;936&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;/videos/{video_id}/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   master.m3u8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   manifest.mpd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   360p/segment1.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   360p/segment2.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   720p/segment1.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   720p/segment2.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;938&quot; data-end=&quot;1236&quot;&gt;When a user clicks a video, the client first requests the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;996&quot; data-end=&quot;1026&quot;&gt;manifest file from the CDN&lt;/strong&gt;, which is cached at edge locations. The manifest tells the video player which resolutions and segment URLs are available. Based on the user’s bandwidth, the player dynamically selects the appropriate segments.&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1238&quot; data-end=&quot;1253&quot;&gt;So the flow is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1255&quot; data-end=&quot;1322&quot;&gt;Client → CDN → Manifest File (from object storage) → Video Segments&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1324&quot; data-end=&quot;1411&quot;&gt;This design allows &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1343&quot; data-end=&quot;1409&quot;&gt;efficient caching, scalability, and adaptive bitrate streaming&lt;/strong&gt;.”&lt;/p&gt;" link="&lt;p data-start=&quot;85&quot; data-end=&quot;458&quot;&gt;“The &lt;strong data-start=&quot;90&quot; data-end=&quot;108&quot;&gt;manifest files&lt;/strong&gt; used for adaptive streaming (HLS &lt;code data-start=&quot;142&quot; data-end=&quot;149&quot;&gt;.m3u8&lt;/code&gt; or DASH &lt;code data-start=&quot;158&quot; data-end=&quot;164&quot;&gt;.mpd&lt;/code&gt;) are stored in the same &lt;strong data-start=&quot;189&quot; data-end=&quot;207&quot;&gt;object storage&lt;/strong&gt; where the encoded video segments are stored. Large video platforms such as &lt;strong data-start=&quot;283&quot; data-end=&quot;324&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;YouTube&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; typically use distributed object storage like &lt;strong data-start=&quot;371&quot; data-end=&quot;412&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Google Cloud Storage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong data-start=&quot;416&quot; data-end=&quot;457&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Amazon S3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;460&quot; data-end=&quot;748&quot;&gt;During the video processing pipeline, after transcoding the raw video into multiple resolutions (for example 360p, 720p, 1080p), the system splits the video into small segments. At the same time, it generates the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;673&quot; data-end=&quot;690&quot;&gt;manifest file&lt;/strong&gt; which lists all available bitrates and segment locations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;750&quot; data-end=&quot;796&quot;&gt;The storage structure usually looks like this:&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;798&quot; data-end=&quot;936&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;/videos/{video_id}/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   master.m3u8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   manifest.mpd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   360p/segment1.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   360p/segment2.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   720p/segment1.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;   720p/segment2.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;938&quot; data-end=&quot;1236&quot;&gt;When a user clicks a video, the client first requests the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;996&quot; data-end=&quot;1026&quot;&gt;manifest file from the CDN&lt;/strong&gt;, which is cached at edge locations. The manifest tells the video player which resolutions and segment URLs are available. Based on the user’s bandwidth, the player dynamically selects the appropriate segments.&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1238&quot; data-end=&quot;1253&quot;&gt;So the flow is:&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1255&quot; data-end=&quot;1322&quot;&gt;Client → CDN → Manifest File (from object storage) → Video Segments&lt;/p&gt;&#xa;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1324&quot; data-end=&quot;1411&quot;&gt;This design allows &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1343&quot; data-end=&quot;1409&quot;&gt;efficient caching, scalability, and adaptive bitrate streaming&lt;/strong&gt;.”&lt;/p&gt;" id="5NoyTFmbiUV2HVWiRSmj-47">
          <mxCell parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" vertex="1">
            <mxGeometry height="490" width="550" x="1670" y="2450" as="geometry" />
          </mxCell>
        </UserObject>
        <mxCell id="5NoyTFmbiUV2HVWiRSmj-48" edge="1" parent="1" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;rounded=0;" value="">
          <mxGeometry height="50" relative="1" width="50" as="geometry">
            <Array as="points">
              <mxPoint x="1120" y="3030" />
              <mxPoint x="1470" y="2960" />
            </Array>
            <mxPoint x="970" y="2510" as="sourcePoint" />
            <mxPoint x="1510" y="2730" as="targetPoint" />
          </mxGeometry>
        </mxCell>
        <UserObject label="&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;4964&quot; data-end=&quot;4992&quot;&gt;Step 5 — Segment fetching&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;4994&quot; data-end=&quot;5017&quot;&gt;Video segments fetched:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;5019&quot; data-end=&quot;5049&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Client → CDN → Storage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;5051&quot; data-end=&quot;5059&quot;&gt;Example:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;5061&quot; data-end=&quot;5107&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;segment_1.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;segment_2.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;segment_3.ts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;5109&quot; data-end=&quot;5128&quot;&gt;Each = 2–4 seconds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;5135&quot; data-end=&quot;5173&quot;&gt;Step 6 — Adaptive bitrate switching&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;5175&quot; data-end=&quot;5194&quot;&gt;If bandwidth drops:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;5196&quot; data-end=&quot;5219&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div