        <mxCell id="5NoyTFmbiUV2HVWiRSmj-104" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="&lt;p data-start=&quot;140&quot; data-end=&quot;369&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;371&quot; data-end=&quot;616&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;I would use a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;392&quot; data-end=&quot;434&quot;&gt;relational or distributed SQL database&lt;/strong&gt; such as &lt;strong data-start=&quot;443&quot; data-end=&quot;484&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;Google Spanner&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; or &lt;strong data-start=&quot;488&quot; data-end=&quot;529&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;hover:entity-accent entity-underline inline cursor-pointer align-baseline&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;whitespace-normal&quot;&gt;CockroachDB&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; to store the &lt;strong data-start=&quot;543&quot; data-end=&quot;575&quot;&gt;user–video like relationship&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;br data-start=&quot;576&quot; data-end=&quot;579&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;This table usually has a schema like:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;pre class=&quot;overflow-visible! px-0!&quot; data-start=&quot;618&quot; data-end=&quot;682&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative w-full my-4&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full min-h-0 min-w-0&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;border border-token-border-light border-radius-3xl corner-superellipse/1.1 rounded-3xl&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;h-full w-full border-radius-3xl bg-token-bg-elevated-secondary corner-superellipse/1.1 overflow-clip rounded-3xl lxnfua_clipPathFallback&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pointer-events-none absolute end-1.5 top-1 z-2 md:end-2 md:top-1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pt-3&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;relative z-0 flex max-w-full&quot;&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;code-block-viewer&quot; dir=&quot;ltr&quot; class=&quot;q9tKkq_viewer cm-editor z-10 light:cm-light dark:cm-light flex h-full w-full flex-col items-stretch ͼk ͼy&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-scroller&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;cm-content q9tKkq_readonly&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;likes(user_id, video_id)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span&gt;PRIMARY KEY (user_id, video_id)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;684&quot; data-end=&quot;795&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1323&quot; data-end=&quot;1354&quot;&gt;So the overall architecture is:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1356&quot; data-end=&quot;1448&quot;&gt;Client → API → Like Service → Redis (fast counter) → Distributed SQL DB (persistent mapping)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;1450&quot; data-end=&quot;1583&quot;&gt;This design combines &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1471&quot; data-end=&quot;1529&quot;&gt;fast writes, duplicate prevention, and durable storage&lt;/strong&gt;, which is necessary for large-scale video platforms.”&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="780" width="560" x="1900" y="4225" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
